 We identified an issue that limited the number of active connections to one of our servers. The root cause was a kernel-level restriction on the maximum number of open files (file descriptors), which also affects network sockets.
Impact:
 The limitation caused a temporary reduction in the number of simultaneous connections the server could handle, potentially affecting availability for some users.
Resolution:
 The kernel and system-level limits for open files were increased to ensure sufficient capacity for concurrent connections. After applying the changes and restarting the affected services, the system returned to normal operation.
